"sendingSystem\": \"Cloudia Kilpailutus\", \"estimatedValue\": null, \"expirationDate\": \"2026-10-06T09:00:00Z\", \"parentNoticeId\": null, \"circularEconomy\": false, \"endUserInvolved\": true, \"isEuProcurement\": true, \"noticeOjsNumber\": \"\", \"contractFolderId\": \"c9f32bf8-bf1f-4bb6-886a-cb09f75ee70e\", \"descriptionOther\": \"\", \"organisationType\": \"ra\", \"previousEFormsId\": [], \"tedPublicationId\": null, \"tenderingInHilma\": false, \"previousSearchIds\": [], \"organisationNameEn\": \"\", \"organisationNameFi\": \"Kanta-Hämeen hyvinvointialue\", \"organisationNameSv\": \"\", \"solutionNewToBuyer\": false, \"employmentCondition\": false, \"organisationAddress\": \"PL 39 13101 Hämeenlinna FIN\", \"procurementTypeCode\": \"services\", \"winnerOrganisations\": \"\", \"innovationConsidered\": true, \"organisationNutsCode\": \"FI1C2\", \"previousFullEFormsId\": [], \"previousNoticeNumber\": [], \"isNationalProcurement\": false, \"justWorkingConditions\": false, \"organisationNameOther\": \"\", \"organisationDepartment\": \"\", \"listedGreenCriteriaUsed\": null, \"noticeResultTotalAmount\": null, \"oldProcurementProjectId\": 0, \"procurementDocumentsUrl\": \"https://tarjouspalvelu.fi/khshp?id=626434&tpk=fab6d445-36b7-4693-adcc-47a51b193539\", \"previousContractFolderId\": [], \"previousTedPublicationId\": [], \"sustainableFoodProduction\": false, \"energyEfficiencyConsidered\": false, \"includesFrameworkAgreement\": false, \"smeParticipationConsidered\": true, \"refOldNoticeTedPublicationId\": null, \"solutionNewToMarketOrIndustry\": false, \"isPrivateSmallValueProcurement\": false, \"howManyOpportunitiesIsEstimated\": null, \"includesDynamicPurcharingSystem\": false, \"isNationalSmallValueProcurement\": false, \"noticeResultTotalAmountCurrency\": null, \"organisationNationalRegistrationNumber\": \"3221307-8\", \"overallMaximumFrameworkContractsAmount\": null, \"overallMaximumFrameworkContractsCurrency\": null, \"overallApproximateFrameworkContractsAmount\": null, \"overallApproximateFrameworkContractsCurrency\": null}',40,NULL,'2026-09-06 10:59:36','2026-09-06 10:59:36');
INSERT INTO `tenders` (`id`, `external_id`, `source`, `type`, `status`, `title`, `description`, `contracting_authority`, `company_size`, `industry_area_id`, `location_id`, `published_date`, `deadline_date`, `estimated_value`, `currency`, `source_url`, `cpv_codes`, `keywords`, `buyer_email`, `buyer_phone`, `pdf_urls`, `raw_data`, `opportunity_score`, `related_tender_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES (629,'2026-056325','HILMA','RFI','OPEN','Electrochemical atomic force microscopy device','Electrochemical atomic force microscopy device Electrochemical atomic force microscopy device: 1) non-resonant sinusoidal-oscillating imaging mode (nroIM): a. Pure vertical z-modulation of the cantilever; amplitudes (from < 1 nm to > 250 nm) and frequencies (from 125 Hz up to 2 kHz) freely selectable. b. In each contacting cycle, a direct determination of the maximum contact force (force setpoint) takes place in real time, where upon all control parameters are automatically and continuously optimized. Force setpoint minimum down to 10 pN. Stable imaging also for \"negative force setpoints\", i.e., below the baseline of the free force curve. c. Effective line rate >= 2 Hz at 512 pixel/line for all force setpoints possible. d. Suited for cantilevers with spring constants from < 0.001 N/m to > 500 N/m. e. Topography, DMT modulus, adhesion, energy dissipation, force setpoint error and deformation are measured and displayed simultaneously (location and time) and in real time. f. Lateral resolution down to atomic defects in lattice is possible. g. The tip-sample force interaction is continuously displayed in real time during the imaging process. h. This mode can be operated without any limitation of functionality with liquid cells, heating cells, EC cell, etc. The change of deflection signal due to cantilever drift is automatically and continuously eliminated (drift, e.g., induced by change of temperature or other environmental conditions). 2) System should be temperature controlled to minimize thermal drift: sensor in scanner and bridge with feedback loop to have scanner + bridge at similar temperature. Availability to heat from ambient to 35 deg. C. 3) System must be: a. Low-z-noise (< / = 40 pm RMS) atomic force microscope (AFM) with closed-loop tip-scanner (in all 3 axes) >= 85 um x 85 um x 9.5 um XYZ. b. Large sample space, capable to integrate heavy (> 5 kg) additional components (e.g., Nanoprober, customized sample holders, external magnetic fields). c. Motorized 150 mm x 150 mm sample stage. d. Extensive set of resonant, non-resonant and non-resonant oscillating imaging modes. The non-resonant, sinusoidal-oscillating imaging mode (nroIM) with freely selectable i) pure vertical z-modulation of the cantilever (amplitudes from < 1 nm to > 250 nm) and ii) frequencies from 125 Hz up to 2 kHz, WITH automated, continuous contact force dependent imaging gains optimization. e. Enhanced scan parameter optimization algorithms that continuously monitor and automatically optimize key feedback-loop parameters (gains, setpoint) for all 3 imaging modes (contact, resonant and non-resonant oscillating). Algorithms are also based on a trace-retrace correlation score. User sets scan size, scan rate and pixel density, then selects engage and system sets and automatically controls feedback settings during scanning continuously. f. Extensive set of piezo force microscopy (PFM) imaging and spectroscopy modes volume spectroscopy (hyperspectral mapping modes) of PFM signals (frequency sweep on large bandwidth to get contact resonance frequency and eigenmode (amplitude/phase versus voltage) simultaneously to topography and mechanical properties, further referred to as dataCUBE modes. g. Torsional resonance mode to acquire dynamic friction signal. Mode has proven to high-resolution image moire pattern of stacked 2D materials. h. Nano-electrical imaging of surface potential (KPFM) in non-resonant, sinusoidal-oscillating imaging mode. 4) Sample handling and automation: a. Accessible sample space >/= 150 mm x 150 mm x 18 mm XYZ, up to 45 mm height. b. Motorized (minimum 150 mm x 150 mm) and programable sample stage, with vacuum sample hold down. c. Vertical, software controlled and automated AFM-tip engage functionality.,','Aalto University Foundation sr','ANY',1,4,NULL,NULL,NULL,'EUR','https://www.hankintailmoitukset.fi/fi/notice/2026-056325','[\"38000000\"]','[\"force\", \"imaging\", \"resonant\", \"sample\", \"mode\", \"atomic\", \"oscillating\", \"continuously\", \"modes\", \"microscopy\", \"contact\", \"setpoint\", \"time\", \"automatically\", \"electrochemical\", \"device\", \"sinusoidal\", \"vertical\", \"cantilever\", \"real\"]',NULL,NULL,'[{\"url\": \"https://www.hankintailmoitukset.fi/fi/notice/2026-056325\", \"name\": \"HILMA Notice\"}]','{\"id\": \"EF-56325\", \"lots\": [], \"type\": \"25\", \"isPlan\": false, \"planId\": 0, \"titleEn\": \"Electrochemical atomic force microscopy device\", \"titleFi\": \"\", \"titleSv\": \"\", \"cpvCodes\": \"38000000\", \"currency\": null, \"deadline\": null, \"eFormsId\": \"a267b116-a3e9-41e2-8297-9ef896b6ee64\", \"isEForms\": true, \"mainType\": \"PriorInformationNotices\", \"noticeId\": 56325, \"lowCarbon\": null, \"nutsCodes\": \"FI1B1\", \"titleOther\": \"\", \"isCancelled\": false, \"procedureId\": 36757, \"biodiversity\": null, \"dateModified\": \"2026-09-06T09:05:04.317Z\", \"fullEFormsId\": \"a267b116-a3e9-41e2-8297-9ef896b6ee64-01\", \"noticeNumber\": \"2026-056325\", \"@search.score\": 1.0, \"codeOfConduct\": null, \"datePublished\": \"2026-09-06T09:05:04.312Z\", \"descriptionEn\": \"Electrochemical atomic force microscopy device Electrochemical atomic force microscopy device:\\n\\n1) non-resonant sinusoidal-oscillating imaging mode (nroIM):\\n\\na. Pure vertical z-modulation of the cantilever; amplitudes (from < 1 nm to > 250 nm) and frequencies (from 125 Hz up to 2 kHz) freely selectable.\\n\\nb. In each contacting cycle, a direct determination of the maximum contact force (force setpoint) takes place in real time, where upon all control parameters are automatically and continuously optimized. Force setpoint minimum down to 10 pN. Stable imaging also for \\\"negative force setpoints\\\", i.e., below the baseline of the free force curve.\\n\\nc. Effective line rate >= 2 Hz at 512 pixel/line for all force setpoints possible.\\n\\nd. Suited for cantilevers with spring constants from < 0.001 N/m to > 500 N/m.\\n\\ne. Topography, DMT modulus, adhesion, energy dissipation, force setpoint error and deformation are measured and displayed simultaneously (location and time) and in real time.\\n\\nf. Lateral resolution down to atomic defects in lattice is possible.\\n\\ng. The tip-sample force interaction is continuously displayed in real time during the imaging process.\\n\\nh. This mode can be operated without any limitation of functionality with liquid cells, heating cells, EC cell, etc. The change of deflection signal due to cantilever drift is automatically and continuously eliminated (drift, e.g., induced by change of temperature or other environmental conditions).\\n\\n2) System should be temperature controlled to minimize thermal drift: sensor in scanner and bridge with feedback loop to have scanner + bridge at similar temperature. Availability to heat from ambient to 35 deg. C.\\n\\n3) System must be:\\n\\na. Low-z-noise (< / = 40 pm RMS) atomic force microscope (AFM) with closed-loop tip-scanner (in all 3 axes) >= 85 um x 85 um x 9.5 um XYZ.\\n\\nb. Large sample space, capable to integrate heavy (> 5 kg) additional components (e.g., Nanoprober, customized sample holders, external magnetic fields).\\n\\nc. Motorized 150 mm x 150 mm sample stage.\\n\\nd. Extensive set of resonant, non-resonant and non-resonant oscillating imaging modes. The non-resonant, sinusoidal-oscillating imaging mode (nroIM) with freely selectable i) pure vertical z-modulation of the cantilever (amplitudes from < 1 nm to > 250 nm) and ii) frequencies from 125 Hz up to 2 kHz, WITH automated, continuous contact force dependent imaging gains optimization.\\n\\ne. Enhanced scan parameter optimization algorithms that continuously monitor and automatically optimize key feedback-loop parameters (gains, setpoint) for all 3 imaging modes (contact, resonant and non-resonant oscillating). Algorithms are also based on a trace-retrace correlation score. User sets scan size, scan rate and pixel density, then selects engage and system sets and automatically controls feedback settings during scanning continuously.\\n\\nf. Extensive set of piezo force microscopy (PFM) imaging and spectroscopy modes volume spectroscopy (hyperspectral mapping modes) of PFM signals (frequency sweep on large bandwidth to get contact resonance frequency and eigenmode (amplitude/phase versus voltage) simultaneously to topography and mechanical properties, further referred to as dataCUBE modes.\\n\\ng. Torsional resonance mode to acquire dynamic friction signal. Mode has proven to high-resolution image moire pattern of stacked 2D materials.\\n\\nh. Nano-electrical imaging of surface potential (KPFM) in non-resonant, sinusoidal-oscillating imaging mode.\\n\\n4) Sample handling and automation:\\n\\na. Accessible sample space >/= 150 mm x 150 mm x 18 mm XYZ, up to 45 mm height.\\n\\nb. Motorized (minimum 150 mm x 150 mm) and programable sample stage, with vacuum sample hold down.\\n\\nc. Vertical, software controlled and automated AFM-tip engage functionality.,\", \"descriptionFi\": \"\", \"descriptionSv\": \"\", \"isCorrigendum\": false, \"linkedNotices\": \"\", \"procedureType\": \"neg-wo-call\", \"sendingSystem\": \"Cloudia Kilpailutus\", \"estimatedValue\": null, \"expirationDate\": \"2027-03-06T09:05:04.312Z\", \"parentNoticeId\": null, \"circularEconomy\": null, \"endUserInvolved\": null, \"isEuProcurement\": true, \"noticeOjsNumber\": \"\", \"contractFolderId\": \"32e0f879-0e21-4cc7-bc34-d8899c5b2019\", \"descriptionOther\": \"\", \"organisationType\": null, \"previousEFormsId\": [], \"tedPublicationId\": null, \"tenderingInHilma\": false, \"previousSearchIds\": [], \"organisationNameEn\": \"Aalto University Foundation sr\", \"organisationNameFi\": \"\", \"organisationNameSv\": \"\", \"solutionNewToBuyer\": null, \"employmentCondition\": null, \"organisationAddress\": \" 00076 AALTO FIN\", \"procurementTypeCode\": \"supplies\", \"winnerOrganisations\": null, \"innovationConsidered\": null, \"organisationNutsCode\": \"FI1B1\", \"previousFullEFormsId\": [], \"previousNoticeNumber\": [], \"isNationalProcurement\": false, \"justWorkingConditions\": null, \"organisationNameOther\": \"\", \"organisationDepartment\": \"\", \"listedGreenCriteriaUsed\": null, \"noticeResultTotalAmount\": null, \"oldProcurementProjectId\": 0, \"procurementDocumentsUrl\": null, \"previousContractFolderId\": [], \"previousTedPublicationId\": [], \"sustainableFoodProduction\": null, \"energyEfficiencyConsidered\": null, \"includesFrameworkAgreement\": null, \"smeParticipationConsidered\": null, \"refOldNoticeTedPublicationId\": null, \"solutionNewToMarketOrIndustry\": null, \"isPrivateSmallValueProcurement\": false, \"howManyOpportunitiesIsEstimated\": null, \"includesDynamicPurcharingSystem\": null, \"isNationalSmallValueProcurement\": false, \"noticeResultTotalAmountCurrency\": null, \"organisationNationalRegistrationNumber\": \"2228357-4\", \"overallMaximumFrameworkContractsAmount\": null, \"overallMaximumFrameworkContractsCurrency\": null, \"overallApproximateFrameworkContractsAmount\": null, \"overallApproximateFrameworkContractsCurrency\": null}',70,NULL,'2026-09-06 10:59:36','2026-09-06 10:59:36');
INSERT INTO `tenders` (`id`, `external_id`, `source`, `type`, `status`, `title`, `description`, `contracting_authority`, `company_size`, `industry_area_id`, `location_id`, `published_date`, `deadline_date`, `estimated_value`, `currency`, `source_url`, `cpv_codes`, `keywords`, `buyer_email`, `buyer_phone`, `pdf_urls`, `raw_data`, `opportunity_score`, `related_tender_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES (630,'2026-056324','HILMA','RFP','OPEN','Large Cancer Panel Test','The HUS Group (also \"the contracting entity\", \"the Client\" or “HUS”) requests tenders for a large cancer panel test for HUS Diagnostic Center. The procurement includes also data analysis software for reporting clinically significant variants, copy number alterations and gene fusions. The software can be offered by the same provider as the large cancer panel test or from a partner company (offer as a group or appeal to a subcontractor\'s resources), but it needs to be included in the same tender. The software will be procured for the entire lifecycle of the assay. The procurement consist of gene panels and reagents (also \"products\") and data analysis software (also \"services\", e.g. information system provided as Software as a Service). Laboratory of Genetics at HUS (Helsinki University Hospital) Diagnostic Center is an SFS-EN ISO 15189:2022 accredited laboratory providing diagnostic genetic testing services to all patients at Helsinki and Uusimaa Hospital District. The laboratory operates as a health institution capable of validating in-house developed tests as required by the CE-IVD regulation. The services include analysis of both constitutional samples and malignancies. The laboratory provides sequencing services mainly using local sequencing capacity (Illumina NovaSeq 6000, NovaSeq X Plus, Ion GeneStudio S5 Prime equipment). The large cancer panel test is intended for detection of small nucleotide variants (SNVs), indels, gene fusions, copy number variations (CNVs), microsatellite instability (MSI), homologous recombination deficiency (HRD), and tumor mutation burden (TMB) relevant for the genetic profiling of solid tumor samples and/or hematological malignancies as well as plasma samples for cfDNA analysis. Sequencing of the samples is carried out using Illumina NovaSeq sequencers (Illumina NovaSeq 6000 and NovaSeq X Plus). The number of cancer panel tests performed annually is estimated to be between 2500-3000. The procurement is divided into LOT A and LOT B: LOT A - This lot includes gene panel solutions for in-house NGS testing of solid tumors and hematological malignancies, including library preparation reagents, target enrichment reagents defining the panel content, panel-specific reagents, data analysis software, and instructions for use. Sequencing reagents, flow cells, sequencing instruments, and testing services are not included in this procurement. - This test is based on analysis of total nucleic acids (RNA and/or DNA) extracted from paraffin embedded specimens and/or fresh-frozen specimens - This lot includes an option for special gene panel and reagents for salivary gland tumors with data analysis software - This lot includes an an option for a custom gene panel and reagents with data analysis software - The HUS Group will decide separately on the use of the options LOT B Important Information Concerning Lot B of the Procurement Procedure The Contracting Authority has decided to discontinue Lot B of the procurement procedure.During the procurement procedure, it became apparent that substantial amendments are required to the subject matter of Lot B and the related procurement documents. As these amendments cannot be implemented through a corrigendum without jeopardising the equal and non-discriminatory treatment of tenderers, the Contracting Authority has decided to discontinue Lot B.Lot B will be re-tendered through a separate procurement procedure. A new contract notice and new procurement documents for Lot B will be published separately.Please note that LOT A is still continuing the tendering process. - This lot includes gene panel solutions for in-house NGS testing of cell-free DNA, including library preparation reagents, target enrichment reagents defining the panel content, panel-specific reagents, data analysis software, and instructions for use. Sequencing reagents, flow cells, sequencing instruments, and testing services are not included in this procurement - This test is based on analysis of cell-free DNA from plasma samples NOTE: For LOT A, the tenderer may offer a catalog panel, a combination of catalog panels, or a custom solution to meet the DNA and RNA requirements. For hematological malignancies, only a panel for DNA is requested. Panel for salivary gland tumors and custom panel are requested as an option. NOTE: FOR LOT A and LOT B, the tender needs to include all the reagents required to perform the assay, including library preparation reagents, indexing adapters and target enrichment reagents (or equivalent). Nucleic acid extraction reagents, library quantification reagents and sequencer reagents are excluded from the tender. The subject of the procurement and its requirements are described in more detail in the call for tender and its appendices. The tenderer can submit a tender to either one or both of the LOTS A and LOT B. The tenderer can be awarded the contract to either one or both tendered lots. The contrcting entity selects one (1) supplier for each lot and will enter into an agreement with the winning supplier. The estimated start for the contract period is autumn-winter 2026. The contracting entity recieves a right to test use tendered panels and softwares after the deadline for receiving the tenders. The procurement volumes presented in the call for tenders are estimates, and the contract does not constitute a mandatory purchase obligation for the contrcting entity or an exclusive right for the supplier to provide the product., LOT A: Panels for Solid Tumors and Hematological Malignancies with Data Analysis Software The subject of the procurement and its requirements are described in more detail in the call for tender and its appendices., LOT B: CfDNA Panel Test with Data Analysis Software Important Information Concerning Lot B of the Procurement Procedure The Contracting Authority has decided to discontinue Lot B of the procurement procedure.During the procurement procedure, it became apparent that substantial amendments are required to the subject matter of Lot B and the related procurement documents. As these amendments cannot be implemented through a corrigendum without jeopardising the equal and non-discriminatory treatment of tenderers, the Contracting Authority has decided to discontinue Lot B.Lot B will be re-tendered through a separate procurement procedure. A new contract notice and new procurement documents for Lot B will be published separately.Please note that LOT A is still continuing the tendering process. The subject of the procurement and its requirements are described in more detail in the call for tender and its appendices.,','HUS Group','SME',3,4,NULL,NULL,NULL,'EUR','https://www.hankintailmoitukset.fi/fi/notice/2026-056324','[\"33000000\", \"48000000\", \"72000000\"]','[\"procurement\", \"panel\", \"reagents\", \"analysis\", \"software\", \"test\", \"data\", \"procedure\", \"gene\", \"tender\", \"sequencing\", \"contracting\", \"services\", \"cancer\", \"includes\", \"testing\", \"samples\", \"malignancies\", \"novaseq\", \"subject\"]',NULL,NULL,'[{\"url\": \"https://tarjouspalvelu.fi/huslogistiikka?id=572070&tpk=f846dc2e-2626-4867-91e2-dff2eb40c0eb\", \"name\": \"Procurement Documents\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.hankintailmoitukset.fi/fi/notice/2026-056324\", \"name\": \"HILMA Notice\"}]','{\"id\": \"EF-56324\", \"lots\": [{\"id\": \"LOT-0001\", \"titleEn\": \"LOT A: Panels for Solid Tumors and Hematological Malignancies with Data Analysis Software\", \"titleFi\": \"\", \"titleSv\": \"\", \"cpvCodes\": \"3300